{"data": [{"author_id": "1519325143679799296", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:13:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118511989920326108"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118511989920326108", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Your speak look like donald trump, are you Donald Trump relatives?", "url": "https://x.com/stropurbo/status/2118511989920326108"}, {"author_id": "17065524", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:55:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118507621355528272"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118507621355528272", "note_tweet": {"text": "Watching this after this week's usage squeeze.\n\nThe change that actually moved the needle for me wasn't a prompt trick, it was killing idle routines.\n\nEvery scheduled run hits the same weekly pool. \n\nSpecialized bots stay. Hourly check-ins go.\n\nCurious which of your 7 is the biggest saver for a multi-bot shop."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Watching this after this week's usage squeeze.\n\nThe change that actually moved the needle for me wasn't a prompt trick, it was killing idle routines.\n\nEvery scheduled run hits the same weekly pool. \n\nSpecialized bots stay. Hourly check-ins go.\n\nCurious which of your 7 is the", "url": "https://x.com/Stan_Timek/status/2118507621355528272"}, {"author_id": "7090302", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:51:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118506513237205233"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118506513237205233", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn You can also just buy more.", "url": "https://x.com/davidjkon/status/2118506513237205233"}, {"author_id": "1052710502818697216", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:33:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118502033963782499"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118502033963782499", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn My butler bot hands tasks to specialist bots, so each one stays narrow. Curious if routine schedules made your list, since checking too often seems like an easy way to burn usage.", "url": "https://x.com/Neverguiltyy/status/2118502033963782499"}, {"author_id": "2062384132697817088", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:32:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118501687019356419"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118501687019356419", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn My grok bot has dropped his intelligence.", "url": "https://x.com/StarSourceH/status/2118501687019356419"}, {"author_id": "1283397399642161152", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:24:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118499778233618454"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118499778233618454", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Spinning up more bots &gt; one overloaded one. The token math is so backwards otherwise", "url": "https://x.com/XylographerX/status/2118499778233618454"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2118402567994834944"], "media_source_tweet_id": ["2118402980340961507"]}, "author_id": "4872216436", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:17:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118498030005465490"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/0ttX8SzlMg", "end": 1229, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AlexFinn/status/2118402980340961507/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118402567994834944", "start": 1206, "url": "https://t.co/0ttX8SzlMg"}]}, "id": "2118498030005465490", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/AlexFinn/statu…", "end": 1229, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AlexFinn/status/2118402980340961507/video/1", "start": 1206, "url": "https://t.co/0ttX8SzlMg"}]}, "text": "7 FREE Keys to Get More Useage Out of Grok Bot\nfrom Grok Bot reviewing Alex's great video:\n\n'Audit your bots (0:58). Delete the bots you don't use. A long roster costs usage on every message. In his demo, he had 30 bots but used only about 6.\n\nAudit your routines (2:45). Routines are easy to create and easy to forget, so cut the ones you don't need. He claims this can save about 80% of daily usage. That's his number, not one I've checked.\n\nUse Claude Code or Codex for coding (3:39). Install one of these coding tools on the bot's computer and have the bot code with it instead of cloud coding agents, which he says use more.\n\nDrop group chats where several agents review each other's work (5:14). He says today's models don't need it much anymore, and it burns usage.\n\nAudit your skills (6:27). The bot checks its list of skills on every request, so remove the ones you don't use.\n\nAudit your plugins and connectors (6:36). Same idea: unused connectors still get checked, so uninstall them.\n\nMix and match agents (8:18). Send each kind of task to the agent that's best at it, so no single subscription runs out. His picks are Dots for voice, Muse for social and online shopping, and Duet for coding.' https://t.co/0ttX8SzlMg"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn 7 FREE Keys to Get More Useage Out of Grok Bot\nfrom Grok Bot reviewing Alex's great video:\n\n'Audit your bots (0:58). Delete the bots you don't use. A long roster costs usage on every message. In his demo, he had 30 bots but used only about 6.\n\nAudit your routines (2:45). Routines", "url": "https://x.com/FreeSites_com/status/2118498030005465490"}, {"author_id": "1441744483482161162", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:13:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118497055782142030"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}], "urls": [{"description": "View this shared creation on Muse", "display_url": "muse.ai/s/muse-welcome…", "end": 33, "expanded_url": "https://muse.ai/s/muse-welcome-kit-xbxu6vxdyxkgxotxb/ZU3r9QtDoPvIHwJr_Tv86JhKdsgDl-tNAzeGBQQ5DvY", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118046863278690304/1hotYK4s?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118046863278690304/1hotYK4s?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 10, "status": 200, "title": "Muse Welcome Kit", "unwound_url": "https://muse.ai/s/muse-welcome-kit-xbxu6vxdyxkgxotxb/ZU3r9QtDoPvIHwJr_Tv86JhKdsgDl-tNAzeGBQQ5DvY", "url": "https://t.co/jA7QEVcBmq"}]}, "id": "2118497055782142030", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn https://t.co/jA7QEVcBmq", "url": "https://x.com/MuseGangGen/status/2118497055782142030"}, {"author_id": "1946596497300267008", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:10:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118496257559679385"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118496257559679385", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn I used one bot that has several different bots inside it. Seems to help with my usage. But I am still running out of it by the end of the week", "url": "https://x.com/Redrum_lI/status/2118496257559679385"}, {"author_id": "2116511805199491072", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:10:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118496097551184278"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 13, "id": "1699883504262377472", "start": 0, "username": "YamanekoInfo"}, {"end": 23, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 14, "username": "AlexFinn"}, {"end": 37, "id": "1699883504262377472", "start": 24, "username": "YamanekoInfo"}]}, "id": "2118496097551184278", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118492367754051938", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@YamanekoInfo @AlexFinn @YamanekoInfo that split tends to work when the coordinator only owns routing and Hermes owns the long jobs. Common failure: both touch the same files/session and overwrite each other. Give Hermes a work dir the bot never writes to, plus one status line the bot can poll.", "url": "https://x.com/Duami_ai/status/2118496097551184278"}, {"author_id": "1699883504262377472", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:55:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118492367754051938"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}, {"end": 19, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 10, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118492367754051938", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "text": "@AlexFinn, great video.\n\nI’m planning to try installing Hermes Agent on the Grok Bot’s virtual computer so the bot mainly acts as a coordinator while Hermes handles the actual work and calls out to different models.\n\nIf you’ve already tried something like this and it didn’t work well, I’d really appreciate a heads-up before I go down that path."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn @AlexFinn, great video.\n\nI’m planning to try installing Hermes Agent on the Grok Bot’s virtual computer so the bot mainly acts as a coordinator while Hermes handles the actual work and calls out to different models.\n\nIf you’ve already tried something like this and it didn’t work", "url": "https://x.com/YamanekoInfo/status/2118492367754051938"}, {"author_id": "1369348853414178822", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:52:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118491708828828132"], "id": "2118491708828828132", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1710, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "you can send this to your grok bot and have it implement everything btw", "url": "https://x.com/AlexFinn/status/2118491708828828132"}, {"author_id": "1373662119879569410", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:35:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118487277336986001"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118487277336986001", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn BS", "url": "https://x.com/mike_j2377/status/2118487277336986001"}, {"author_id": "251115196", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:34:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118487123514814599"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118487123514814599", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn People who run out of usage, rethink what you’re using it for. The ones actually making money with it do not complain.", "url": "https://x.com/DukeOfSax/status/2118487123514814599"}, {"author_id": "2060451201125376000", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:54:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477190908239930"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118477190908239930", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn I figured out the hard way not to code with Grokbot but ever since I had Claude audit my bots in the routines usage has been phenomenal. Right up until that little blip we had the other day 😆", "url": "https://x.com/ASaltyVet/status/2118477190908239930"}, {"author_id": "38089493", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:41:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118473711162630257"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118473711162630257", "note_tweet": {"text": "If people want more usage out of Grok Bot, then buy more usage! It’s not like you hit 100% and you have no choices. All the bitching is stupid. If you go to a restaurant and buy your favorite menu item, you get a portion of that item for the price listed on the menu. If you wanted more than that, you don’t bust into the kitchen and beg the cook for more food. YOU PAY FOR MORE FOOD."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 113, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn If people want more usage out of Grok Bot, then buy more usage! It’s not like you hit 100% and you have no choices. All the bitching is stupid. If you go to a restaurant and buy your favorite menu item, you get a portion of that item for the price listed on the menu. If you", "url": "https://x.com/bryan_grayson/status/2118473711162630257"}, {"author_id": "2117887864503422977", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:18:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118468045995688114"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 0, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118468045995688114", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402980340961507", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Nobody should be using 10+ bots", "url": "https://x.com/BotYardCloud/status/2118468045995688114"}, {"author_id": "1264659188", "conversation_id": "2118402980340961507", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:10:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466080465158613"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 13, "id": "1709987537618341888", "start": 0, "username": "BeerCanSand1"}, {"end": 24, "id": "771317869", "start": 14, "username": "Vantekai_"}, {"end": 34, "id": "1369348853414178822", "start": 25, "username": "AlexFinn"}]}, "id": "2118466080465158613", "note_tweet": {"text": "It takes time to implement, and the manual scanning is annoying. But it’s totally worth it once done. I recommend using the scan feature in Google Drive, as it scans with OCR (Optical Character Recognition), which creates a searchable document and enables the bot to analyse the scans quickly, resulting in much less token burn than analysing an image or scanned file without OCR. Enjoy✌️"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118453473712693268", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@BeerCanSand1 @Vantekai_ @AlexFinn It takes time to implement, and the manual scanning is annoying. But it’s totally worth it once done. I recommend using the scan feature in Google Drive, as it scans with OCR (Optical Character Recognition), which creates a searchable document and enables the bot to analyse the", "url": "https://x.com/AuzyMale/status/2118466080465158613"}, {"author_id": "8